# P14B Plane Cut with Fill across a hollow section: a Torus (major 50, minor 25, pivot at its base) moved so the
# world plane Y = 0 runs through its middle; Plane Cut axis Y, World, Keep -, Fill on -> the cap is a ring
# (PlanarComplex nests the outer and inner loops, ConstrainedDelaunay2 fills between them) -> Undo.
Дано run Panel "Open Modeling"
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.3,-0.9,0.3
Дано run Modeling "Create shape tool: Torus"
Дано run Modeling "Create shape: place at the viewport centre"
Дано --subject selection set Translation 0,-25,0
Дано run Entity Torus
Дано run "Level Viewport" "Focus Selected"
Дано run Modeling "Select Elements tool"
Когда run Modeling "Plane Cut axis: Y"
Когда run Modeling "Plane Cut: World: on"
Когда run Modeling "Plane Cut: Keep -: on"
Когда run Modeling "Plane Cut: Fill: on"
Когда run Modeling "Mesh operation: Plane Cut"
Тогда 0_cut the torus is cut flat through its middle; the cap is a ring - filled between the outer and the inner circle - and the centre hole stays open (the floor/grid is seen through it, no triangles across it)
Когда run Action Undo
Тогда-вид 1_undo after Undo the whole uncut torus is back
